os_intfs: provide strscpy() on kernels before 4.3

strscpy() was added in 4.3. The driver uses it in the ethtool get_drvinfo
callback only, and never evaluates the return value, so mapping it onto
strlcpy() is behaviourally equivalent here. Without this the driver does
not build on 4.1 kernels (sf4008).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [driver runs on older kernels than upstream targets]

--- a/os_dep/linux/os_intfs.c
+++ b/os_dep/linux/os_intfs.c
@@ -17,6 +17,12 @@
 #include <drv_types.h>
 #include <hal_data.h>
 
+#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(4, 3, 0))
+/* strscpy() arrived in 4.3. It is only used to copy strings here and
+ * its return value is never checked, so strlcpy() is a safe stand-in. */
+#define strscpy(dest, src, count) strlcpy(dest, src, count)
+#endif
+
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Realtek Wireless Lan Driver");
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Realtek Semiconductor Corp.");
